  "title": "Unified AI-Driven Content Experience on Reddit",
  "summary": "Reddit is rethinking its open-web roots to protect its audience and business, while also integrating AI-powered search features into its platform. This shift aims to enhance accessibility and interactivity by converting text-based posts into multimedia formats.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Reddit is testing video and audio versions of posts to improve accessibility and interactivity.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reddit's CEO Steve Huffman stated that Google's AI-powered search modes do not help with traffic to the platform.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reddit will require users to log in to access its platform, which is expected to change significantly.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
